This repository contains the AGPL-3.0-or-later Android client for Ramflux. It
depends on the BSD-3-Clause Ramflux core workspace maintained in the
ramfluxhq/ramflux repository.

The native build statically links OpenSSL 3.6.3 for the SDK's SQLCipher backend.
OpenSSL is licensed under Apache-2.0; its license is included in the SDK AAR.
The reused Keystore helper retains its BSD-3-Clause SPDX header.

The device-pairing invitation is drawn as a QR code with ZXing core 3.5.4
(com.google.zxing:core, Copyright ZXing authors), licensed under Apache-2.0.
Only the core encoder is linked; no ZXing Android or camera artefact is used.
See third_party/zxing/LICENSE and the project's notices in third_party/zxing/NOTICE.

Media libraries (linked from :core:media and :feature:chat):
- AndroidX Media3 1.11.1 (common, transformer, effect, exoplayer, ui-compose), licensed under Apache-2.0.
- AndroidX Emoji2 emoji picker 1.4.0, licensed under Apache-2.0.
- Bouncy Castle provider 1.78.1 (org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on, Copyright The Legion of the Bouncy
  Castle Inc.), used for BLAKE3 attachment digests and direct conversation ids, licensed under the MIT
  License. See third_party/bouncycastle/LICENSE; the text is also shown in the app's notices.

The Kit icons are vector drawables drawn from Lucide 0.544.0 (Copyright Lucide Contributors, portions
Copyright Cole Bemis as part of Feather), licensed under the ISC License with MIT portions. See
third_party/lucide/LICENSE; the text is also shown in the app's notices.

Bundled UI fonts, both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1:
- Hanken Grotesk, Copyright 2021 The Hanken Grotesk Project Authors. See third_party/hanken-grotesk/OFL.txt.
- JetBrains Mono, Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors. See third_party/jetbrains-mono/OFL.txt.
Chinese text uses the platform Noto Sans CJK font and is not bundled.
